# Mercury Edit 2 — findings by Nemotron 3 Ultra 550B A55B

- Source: Inception Labs (`inception/mercury-edit-2`)
- Date: 2026-11-13 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Mercury Edit 2
- **Short description:** Inception Labs' diffusion-based next-edit prediction model for code autocomplete and multi-line edits, aligned with Kahneman-Tversky Optimization (KTO). Specialized FIM (fill-in-the-middle) and edit endpoint tuning rather than open-ended conversational coding.
- **Provider / access:** Inception Labs API (`inception/mercury-edit-2`), endpoints: `v1/fim/completions` (autocomplete) and `v1/edit/completions` (next-edit suggestions). OpenAI API compatible. No chat completions endpoint.
- **Release / knowledge:** Release date not publicly specified; diffusion-based architecture with KTO alignment; knowledge cutoff not publicly specified.
- **IDs:** `inception/mercury-edit-2` (Inception Labs API); no free ID on OpenCode Zen or OpenRouter.
- **Context window:** 32,000 total (FIM: 32K, NextEdit: 32K) / 8,192 max output (per Inception Labs docs)
- **Modalities:** Text in; text out; specialized for code editing (FIM autocomplete, next-edit diffs). No reasoning effort options, no tool calling, no structured outputs for this model.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-13):** $0.25 / $0.75 per 1M (input / output); $0.025 per 1M cached input. No free tier.
- **Architecture:** Diffusion-based LLM (dLLM) with parallel denoising for multi-line code diffs; KTO-aligned; proprietary.

